{
 "about": "Hand-judged page labels for the per-page structural checks (verifier round 2, 2026-10-20). Only document identity (sha256 of the original PDF, or for a sample built from it by tests/fixtures/make_manual.py the sha256 of its text layers, and the sha256 of the judged Markdown), page numbers, expected reasons and verdicts; no document text. The PDFs and Markdown live in tests/fixtures/manual/ (never committed). Policy: page_dropped = the section holds essentially none of the page's text (at most a heading or a caption; a text-heavy diagram kept as a picture counts as its text); page_partial = it holds some, but clearly less than half of the page's prose (labels inside a figure kept as a picture are not prose); page_misaligned = most of the page's text sits under another page's marker; page_oversized = the section holds another page's text (most of that page's own text, or a whole block of it such as table rows or a paragraph that is not the continuation of a sentence across the page break); ambiguous = no clear verdict, excluded from the scores. split 'dev' = pages the checks were designed or corrected on (it includes the first and second test splits, each measured once and then seen); 'test' = pages sampled after the checks were frozen for the last time. 'note' records a relabelling and its reason.",
